DEEP STRUCTURE: 5-cycles in P_7
======================================================================

P_7 cycle census:
  3-cycles: 14
  5-cycles: 42
  7-cycles (Hamiltonian): 24

5-cycle complements (the 2-element set NOT in each 5-cycle):
  Complement pair distribution: {(3, 6): 2, (0, 4): 2, (0, 1): 2, (0, 6): 2, (2, 6): 2, (2, 4): 2, (0, 2): 2, (1, 4): 2, (3, 4): 2, (0, 5): 2, (2, 3): 2, (1, 2): 2, (1, 5): 2, (4, 6): 2, (5, 6): 2, (1, 6): 2, (1, 3): 2, (0, 3): 2, (4, 5): 2, (2, 5): 2, (3, 5): 2}
  Uniform: True
  Each complement pair appears in 2 5-cycles
  → The 5-cycles form a COMPLEMENTARY design:
    The COMPLEMENTS of 5-blocks are a 2-(7,2,λ') design

Relation between 3-cycles and 5-cycles:
  A 5-cycle on {a,b,c,d,e} avoids pair {f,g}.
  The pair {f,g} forms an arc f→g or g→f.
  Question: does the number of 5-cycles avoiding {f,g}
  relate to the number of 3-cycles THROUGH {f,g}?

      pair  3-cyc thru  5-cyc thru  5-cyc avoid   sum
  --------------------------------------------------
  (0,1)              2          20           22    22
  (0,2)              2          20           22    22
  (0,3)              2          20           22    22
  (0,4)              2          20           22    22
  (0,5)              2          20           22    22
  (0,6)              2          20           22    22
  (1,2)              2          20           22    22
  (1,3)              2          20           22    22
  (1,4)              2          20           22    22
  (1,5)              2          20           22    22
  (1,6)              2          20           22    22
  (2,3)              2          20           22    22
  (2,4)              2          20           22    22
  (2,5)              2          20           22    22
  (2,6)              2          20           22    22
  (3,4)              2          20           22    22
  (3,5)              2          20           22    22
  (3,6)              2          20           22    22
  (4,5)              2          20           22    22
  (4,6)              2          20           22    22
  (5,6)              2          20           22    22

  OBSERVATION: c₃(pair) + c₅(pair) = ? Check if constant
  Sums: [22] → CONSTANT
  λ₃ + λ₅ = 22 = constant across all pairs!
  This means: odd-cycle incidence is CONSERVED.
  A pair in more 3-cycles has correspondingly fewer 5-cycles.

