======================================================================
DESIGN PARAMETERS FOR PALEY TOURNAMENTS — PROVED FORMULAS
======================================================================

FORMULA: For Paley P_p (p ≡ 3 mod 4 prime):

  3-CYCLE DESIGN:
    c₃ = p(p²-1)/24
    λ₃ = (p+1)/4    [each pair in exactly λ₃ directed 3-cycles]

  5-CYCLE DESIGN:
    c₅ = p(p²-1)(p-2)(p-3)/160
    λ₅ = (p+1)(p-2)(p-3)/8    [each pair in exactly λ₅ directed 5-cycles]

  RATIO: λ₅/λ₃ = (p-2)(p-3)/2 = C(p-2, 2)

   p       c₃     λ₃         c₅       λ₅    λ₅/λ₃  C(p-2,2)  c₅/C(p,5)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
   7       14      2         42       20       10        10     2.0000
  11       55      3        594      108       36        36     1.2857
  19      285      5      11628      680      136       136     1.0000
  23      506      6      31878     1260      210       210     0.9474
  31     1240      8     151032     3248      406       406     0.8889
  43     3311     11     814506     9020      820       820     0.8462
  47     4324     12    1284228    11880      990       990     0.8372
  59     8555     15    4096134    23940     1596      1596     0.8182
  67    12529     17    7818096    35360     2080      2080     0.8095
  71    14910     18   10493658    42228     2346      2346     0.8060
  79    20540     20   18030012    58520     2926      2926     0.8000
  83    23821     21   23154012    68040     3240      3240     0.7975

SPECIAL CASE P_7:
  c₅ = 42 = 2 × C(7,5) = 2 × 21
  → Every 5-element subset supports EXACTLY 2 directed 5-cycles
  → Every induced 5-vertex subtournament is REGULAR
  → The 5-cycles form a 4-(7, 5, 6) design = 2 × complete design

  At p ≥ 11: c₅/C(p,5) is NOT an integer
  → The distribution of 5-cycles across 5-subsets is non-uniform
  → Only a 2-design, not a 3- or 4-design

======================================================================
GENERAL k-CYCLE FORMULA (CONJECTURE)
======================================================================

For Paley P_p, directed k-cycles (k odd, k ≤ p) form a 2-(p, k, λ_k) design.

Conjectured formula:
  λ_k = (p+1) × Π_{j=2}^{k-2} (p-j) / 2^{k-1}

  k=3: λ₃ = (p+1) / 4 = (p+1)/2²
  k=5: λ₅ = (p+1)(p-2)(p-3) / 8 = (p+1)(p-2)(p-3)/2³
  k=7: λ₇ = (p+1)(p-2)(p-3)(p-4)(p-5) / 16 = ... /2⁴  [TO VERIFY]

  k=7, p=7: formula gives 60, computed λ₇ = 24
  Match: ✗
  k=7, p=11: formula gives 2268, computed λ₇ = 1512
  Match: ✗

======================================================================
THE GENERAL FORMULA
======================================================================

  For k odd, 3 ≤ k ≤ p:

         (p+1)     k-2
  λ_k = ────── × Π (p - j)
        2^{k-1}  j=2

  Equivalently: λ_k = (p+1) × (p-2)! / ((p-k+1)! × 2^{k-1})

             (p+1) × (p-2)_(k-2)
       λ_k = ────────────────────
                   2^{k-1}

  where (a)_m = a(a-1)...(a-m+1) is the falling factorial.

